/-!
# KFN: implementations of selected-bit operators and of network steps

* `ClN f`: the clean scratch used by all KFN programs (`KFB.Cl`, `KFG.ClP`, `KFG.ClT`, and the
  block counter `cO`).
* `SImpl r st n T code e dw cost`: on a clean managed state whose data stack starts with a record
  array `zs` (scale `F`, width `w`) representing `xs` (`n` records of `r` entries), `code` leaves
  an array representing `selOpF st n T xs` at scale `F + e`, width `w + dw`, at fine cost
  `cost w`.  This is `KFH.LImpl` with the layout given by record strides (`lImpl_of_sImpl`).
* `RImpl r n st A code e dw cost`: the same for a network operator `A` acting on `W` role streams
  stored one after the other (`flatR X`), through `roleOpF`.
* `RImpl.comp`, `rImpl_list` (a list of steps implements `denListR`), and
  `sImpl_of_rImpl_roleDiag`: an implementation of `roleDiag T` is one of `T` on the
  concatenated streams (strides inside the role blocks, `selOpF_flatR`).
